#lang saffron
;; saffron-lang-plan D7: session protocols still check in a Saffron file.
;;
;; The protocol lives in the ANNOTATION, and D2 keeps annotations legal in
;; Saffron, so the channel's type is `Session[Send[int, Close]]` here exactly
;; as it would be in Turmeric -- `any` never touches it.  Measured: the same
;; TUR-E0211, naming the same protocol state.
;;
;; See tests/fixtures/saffron-static-guarantees-still-hold for why this is
;; pinned: D7's first draft would have removed the feature outright.

(defn go [c : (Session (Send int Close))] 0)

(defn main [] 0)
